 position 1, the Pakistani person must be immediately to the right of the videographer (because if they were to the left, there is no position to the left of position 1).\n  - So, the Pakistani person must be in position 2.\n\nThus:\n- Position 1: Nationality = not Pakistani, so nigerian\n- Position 2: Nationality = pakistani\n\n#### Step 3: Assign remaining attributes.\n- We already assigned:\n  - Position 1: Job = videographer, Nationality = nigerian\n  - Position 2: Movie-Genre = animation, Nationality = pakistani\n\n- Remaining attributes:\n  - Position 1: Movie-Genre must be unique, so if position 2 watches animation, position 1 watches thriller.\n  - Position 2: Job must be unique, so if position 1 is a videographer, position 2 is a freelancer.\n\nSo the full assignments are:\n- Position 1:\n  - Job: videographer\n  - Movie-Genre: thriller\n  - Nationality: nigerian\n- Position 2:\n  - Job: freelancer\n  - Movie-Genre: animation\n  - Nationality: pakistani\n\n#### Step 4: Answer the questions:\n1. What is the job of the person who is Pakistani?\n   - The Pakistani person is in position 2, whose job is freelancer.\n   - Answer: freelancer\n\n2. What is the movie genre of the person who is Pakistani?\n   - The Pakistani person is in position 2, whose movie genre is animation.\n   - Answer: animation\n\n3. What movie genre does the person in position 1 watch?\n   - The person in position 1 watches thriller.\n   - Answer: thriller\n\n4. At what position is the person who is a videographer?\n   - The videographer is in position 1.\n   - Answer: 1\n\n### Final answers in order:\n<solution>freelancer, animation, thriller, 1</solution>\n\nFinal answer: <solution>freelancer, animation, thriller, 1</solution>", "logprobs": [{"token": "Let", "logprob": -0.2441253960132599}, {"token": "'s", "logprob": -0.026079803705215454}, {"token": " analyze", "logprob": -0.5923439264297485}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.024798650294542313}, {"token": " problem", "logprob": -0.36137